<title>UK: Turkey sets 750 mln mark five-year bond, +280 bp.</title>
<headline>Turkey sets 750 mln mark five-year bond, +280 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Deutche Morgan Grenfell and Commerzbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   REPUBLIC OF TURKEY</p>
<p> AMT    750 MLN MARK  COUPON     7.625     MATURITY    05.DEC.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.35    PAY DATE    05.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50 PCT  REOFFER    99.85     SPREAD	+280 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	BA3	 LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  B+	  DENOMS (K) 1-10	SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  TURKEY    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    1.0	 SELL CONC  1.0	 LIST	  0.50</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND SEPT 2001 BUND</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
